A root module that is new to Bazel usually has .tf files and nothing else. The provider lock file is the one artifact the rules need and the source tree may not have yet, so the first steps produce it. Declare the module. A terraform_module is one directory of .tf files. No lock, no deps yet: load("@rules_terraform//terraform:defs.bzl", "terraform_module", "terraform_providers_lock") terraform_module( name = "app", srcs = glob(["*.tf"]),
) # Writes .terraform.lock.hcl next to this BUILD file, for every platform
# in the default set, using the toolchain's terraform. Needs network.
terraform_providers_lock( name = "providers_lock.update", output = ".terraform.lock.hcl", target = ":app",
) Generate the lock and commit it: bazel run //path/to/app:providers_lock.update Rerun it whenever a required_providers block changes. There is no step that runs terraform from your PATH. Declare the module's dependencies in MODULE.bazel, one deps tag per lock file: terraform = use_extension("@rules_terraform//terraform:extensions.bzl", "terraform")
terraform.deps( name = "app_deps", lock = "//path/to/app:.terraform.lock.hcl", roots = ["//path/to/app:main.tf"], # only if main.tf names registry modules
)
use_repo(terraform, "app_deps") Wire the module up and add the workflow targets: load("@rules_terraform//terraform:defs.bzl", "terraform_binary", "terraform_providers_lock_test", "terraform_validate_test") terraform_module( name = "app", srcs = glob(["*.tf"]), deps = ["@app_deps"], # the providers, the lock, and the registry modules
) terraform_binary(name = "terraform", root = ":app") # bazel run //path/to/app:terraform -- plan
terraform_validate_test(name = "validate", target = ":app")
terraform_providers_lock_test( # fails when the lock drifts from the sources name = "providers_lock", lock = ".terraform.lock.hcl", target = ":app",
) Add what the module calls. A local child module is its own terraform_module listed in deps; a registry module comes through the directory being in a deps tag's roots, which the hub above already covers. Both are described under External dependencies and lock files . A repo with several root modules repeats steps 1 to 4 per root, or shares one lock file across roots as the monorepo example does. Add .terraform/ to .gitignore; the rules never write it into the source tree, but a stray native init would. To fetch providers and registry modules, declare a deps tag on the terraform extension (or tofu, for OpenTofu): the lock file for providers, the directories with module blocks for registry modules. terraform = use_extension("@rules_terraform//terraform:extensions.bzl", "terraform")
terraform.deps( name = "app", lock = "//path/to:.terraform.lock.hcl", # providers the lock pins roots = ["//path/to:main.tf"], # registry modules named here
)
use_repo(terraform, "app")

