terraform_test runs the engine's native test framework. Each run block is reported as a JUnit test case through XML_OUTPUT_FILE, so bazel test summaries and CI dashboards show which run failed rather than one opaque target. Terraform writes the report itself with -junit-xml; for OpenTofu, which has no such flag, the runner builds it from the -json-into event stream and keeps that stream too. The lock file and module manifest the test ran against land in the undeclared outputs directory (bazel-testlogs/<pkg>/<name>/test.outputs/). terraform_plan_test runs a real plan and keeps plan.tfplan, plan.json and plan.txt as undeclared outputs, so a plan can be reviewed from CI artefacts. It passes when the plan succeeds, or with expect_no_changes only when the plan is empty. A plan reaches the backend and the provider APIs, so the macro tags the target requires-network; credentials go through --test_env. Providers that work offline (null, local, random) need neither. Plans and state hold sensitive values, so treat those artefacts as you would the state itself. For validation and formatting, use the corresponding test rules: terraform_validate_test( name = "validate_test", target = ":my_module",
) terraform_fmt_test( name = "fmt_test", target = ":my_module",
)
